1
00:05:31,428 --> 00:05:37,428
Get ready for the race of your life.

2
00:11:02,857 --> 00:11:08,857
Driven is a action, drama film directed by Renny Harlin.

3
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:40,285
Talented rookie race-car driver Jimmy Bly has started losing his
focus and begins to slip in the race rankings.

4
00:22:05,714 --> 00:22:11,714
It's no wonder, with the immense pressure being shoveled on him by his overly ambitious
promoter brother as well as Bly's romance with his arch rival's girlfriend Sophia.

5
00:27:37,142 --> 00:27:43,142
With much riding on Bly, car owner Carl Henry brings former
racing star Joe Tanto on board to help Bly.

6
00:33:08,571 --> 00:33:14,571
To drive Bly back to the top of the rankings, Tanto must first deal with the emotional
scars left over from a tragic racing accident which nearly took his life.

7
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Joe Tanto, played by Sylvester Stallone.

8
00:44:11,428 --> 00:44:17,428
Carl Henry, played by Burt Reynolds.

9
00:49:42,857 --> 00:49:48,857
Jimmy Bly, played by Kip Pardue.

10
00:55:14,285 --> 00:55:20,285
Lucretia Clan, played by Stacy Edwards.

11
01:00:45,714 --> 01:00:51,714
Beau Brandenburg, played by Til Schweiger.

12
01:06:17,142 --> 01:06:23,142
Cathy Heguy, played by Gina Gershon.

13
01:11:48,571 --> 01:11:54,571
Driven is a 2001 American sports action film directed by Renny Harlin and
starring Sylvester Stallone, who also wrote and produced.

14
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
The film centers on a young racing driver's effort to win the CART
FedEx Championship Series auto racing championship.

15
01:22:51,428 --> 01:22:57,428
Prior to production, Stallone was seen at many Formula One races, but he was unable to procure enough information about the category due to the
secrecy with which teams protect their cars, so he decided to base the film on the Championship Auto Racing Teams (CART) racing series.

16
01:28:22,857 --> 01:28:28,857
Released on April 27, 2001 by Warner Bros.

17
01:33:54,285 --> 01:34:00,285
Pictures, Driven received generally negative reviews from
critics, and was a commercial failure.

18
01:39:25,714 --> 01:39:31,714
Stallone includes "Driven" in his list of movies he has regretted making.

19
01:44:57,142 --> 01:45:03,142
The film explores themes of career, sports, competition, automobile.

20
01:50:28,571 --> 01:50:34,571
The tone is emotional.
